{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Where does the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/2611cedeaf8ce0f9116398f40349ea222e2b3a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\tan^{-1}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> have inflection points?\n</p><p>\t\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44acda5c119740f66471b21e610f8a11bb7d7772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } x=0  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(B) } x=\\pm \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(C) } x=\\pm 1  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(D) } x=\\pm 2  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(E) } \\text{The curve does not have any inflection points.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"803\" height=\"34\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Inflection points occur whenever the second derivative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc8b3f74bcf7c07fc0bb6e488182f87b42dc507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"19\" /> changes signs. We calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39535be386358c81aaa05b879e929e500c07219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39; = \\frac{1}{1+x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01b006e4950961b7d5e2c0b9b71af495ae8580ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39; = -\\frac{2x}{ \\left(1+x^2\\right)^2 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"133\" height=\"45\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378ef709522ce9a9d91b19214485ae2669967b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"19\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc8b3f74bcf7c07fc0bb6e488182f87b42dc507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"19\" /> is positive for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a68e8aa6ec6f48231ad80a4851f84bacf641b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and is negative for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, the curve has inflection points at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c52781794f84cb85236a865bdbbd3df2e8add5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ x=0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA Hig